## 4. Requested `ModelConfig` fields (verbatim)

### `platform` (field 2)

```proto
  //@@  .. cpp:var:: string platform
  //@@
  //@@     Additional backend-specific configuration for the model.
  //@@     Please refer to the backend documentation on whether this field
  //@@     should be specified.
  //@@
  string platform = 2;
```

### `backend` (field 17)

```proto
  //@@  .. cpp:var:: string backend
  //@@
  //@@     The backend used by the model.
  //@@
  string backend = 17;
```

### `optimization` (field 12)

```proto
  //@@  .. cpp:var:: ModelOptimizationPolicy optimization
  //@@
  //@@     Optimization configuration for the model. If not specified
  //@@     then default optimization policy is used.
  //@@
  ModelOptimizationPolicy optimization = 12;
```

### `instance_group` (field 7)

```proto
  //@@  .. cpp:var:: ModelInstanceGroup instance_group (repeated)
  //@@
  //@@     Instances of this model. If not specified, one instance
  //@@     of the model will be instantiated on each available GPU.
  //@@
  repeated ModelInstanceGroup instance_group = 7;
```

---

## Summary

| Requested item | Present in file? | Where / note |
|---|---|---|
| `ModelOptimizationPolicy` message | ✅ Yes | Fully quoted in Section 2 |
| `OptimizationProfile` message with min/opt/max dims | ❌ **Not present** | No such message exists in this proto |
| Fields defining TensorRT optimization profiles for dynamic shapes | ⚠️ Partial | `ModelInstanceGroup.profile` (selects existing profiles); `ModelOptimizationPolicy.Cuda.GraphSpec` (Shape/LowerBound for CUDA graphs); `ModelTensorReshape` |
| `ModelConfig` → `platform` | ✅ Yes | `string platform = 2;` |
| `ModelConfig` → `backend` | ✅ Yes | `string backend = 17;` |
| `ModelConfig` → `optimization` | ✅ Yes | `ModelOptimizationPolicy optimization = 12;` |
| `ModelConfig` → `instance_group` | ✅ Yes | `repeated ModelInstanceGroup instance_group = 7;` |

**Note:** In this proto file, the classic TensorRT `OptimizationProfile` with `min`/`opt`/`max` per-input dims is **not defined**. That construct is typically expressed in the model's `config.pbtxt` and/or handled at the TensorRT engine level, not in this `model_config.proto` content.
